amcempega.library/--background--             amcempega.library/--background--

    PURPOSE
        Decodes MPEG audio (MPEG-1, MPEG-2 and MPEG-2.5; Layers I, II and
        III) to 16-bit signed PCM, one buffer for each channel. Its
        functions, structures and constants are mpega.library's (version
        2), so a program written for mpega.library works with it: open
        AMCEMPEGANAME instead of "mpega.library".

    USE
        MPEGA_open a stream (a file by name, or through your bitstream
        hook), call MPEGA_decode_frame for each frame's samples until it
        returns MPEGA_ERR_EOF, MPEGA_close it. Only the task that opened a
        stream may use it; different tasks may each have their own.

    MEMORY AND STACK
        About 60 KB a stream (with its default 16 KB buffer and its 16 KB
        stack), from exec.
        The decoding runs on the stream's own 16 KB stack (exec's
        StackSwap), so the caller needs little of its own.

    LICENCE
        The library: GPL-3.0-or-later (libmad inside, GPL-2.0-or-later);
        its source: https://github.com/luvwagn/mpga.library. This
        interface (the headers, the .sfd, this document): MIT.

amcempega.library/MPEGA_close                   amcempega.library/MPEGA_close

    NAME
        MPEGA_close -- a stream closed (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        MPEGA_close(mpega_stream)
                    A0
        VOID MPEGA_close(MPEGA_STREAM *);

    FUNCTION
        Closes the stream (its hook's MPEGA_BSFUNC_CLOSE, or the file) and
        frees it. NULL is ignored.

amcempega.library/MPEGA_decode_frame     amcempega.library/MPEGA_decode_frame

    NAME
        MPEGA_decode_frame -- the next frame decoded (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        samples = MPEGA_decode_frame(mpega_stream, pcm)
        D0                           A0            A1
        LONG MPEGA_decode_frame(MPEGA_STREAM *, WORD *[MPEGA_MAX_CHANNELS]);

    FUNCTION
        Decodes the stream's next frame into pcm[0] (left, or mono) and
        pcm[1] (right, when dec_channels is 2), each MPEGA_PCM_SIZE WORDs:
        at dec_frequency, the stream's rate divided as MPEGA_open chose.
        Damaged frames are passed over. A Xing or Info frame is not sound
        and gives nothing.

    RESULT
        The samples a channel (up to MPEGA_PCM_SIZE); or MPEGA_ERR_EOF at
        the stream's end, MPEGA_ERR_BADFRAME if too many frames in a row
        would not decode, MPEGA_ERR_BADVALUE.

amcempega.library/MPGA_decode_to             amcempega.library/MPGA_decode_to

    NAME
        MPGA_decode_to -- the next frame into the program's buffers (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        samples = MPGA_decode_to(mpega_stream, out)
        D0                       A0            A1
        LONG MPGA_decode_to(MPEGA_STREAM *, struct MpgaOut *);

    FUNCTION
        amcempega.library's own, not mpega.library's (it is after mpega's
        functions in the library's table): as MPEGA_decode_frame, but the
        samples written straight into out's buffers in the format the
        program's output wants, so that it need not copy or convert them
        again, and their peak and the clipped ones counted on the way.
        out->mo_Buffer[] are rings of out->mo_Mask + 1 samples each (a
        power of two; ~0 for buffers that do not wrap), written from
        out->mo_Index on; mo_Index is advanced by the samples written.
            MPGA_FMT_S16   WORDs: [0] left (or mono), [1] right
            MPGA_FMT_S16I  WORDs, left and right interleaved in [0], as
                           AHI's AHIST_S16S (mono: AHIST_M16S); mo_Mask
                           in WORDs, mo_Index in sample frames
            MPGA_FMT_S8    signed bytes for Paula (the high byte):
                           [0] left, [1] right
            MPGA_FMT_S8D   the same, rounded with triangular dither of
                           one 8-bit step
            MPGA_FMT_S14   Paula's 14 bits: [0] and [1] each channel's
                           high byte (signed; at volume 64), [2] and [3]
                           its next 6 bits (0 to 63; at volume 1, each
                           on a channel of its own)
        out->mo_Peak[] is each channel's largest size this frame (0 to
        32767, of the 16-bit sample); out->mo_Clipped is added the
        samples clipped.

    RESULT
        As MPEGA_decode_frame's: the samples a channel, or an error
        (MPEGA_ERR_BADVALUE also for an unknown format or a buffer
        missing).

amcempega.library/MPEGA_find_sync           amcempega.library/MPEGA_find_sync

    NAME
        MPEGA_find_sync -- an MPEG audio frame header found (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        offset = MPEGA_find_sync(buffer, buffer_size)
        D0                       A0      D0
        LONG MPEGA_find_sync(BYTE *, LONG);

    FUNCTION
        Looks for a valid MPEG audio frame header in the buffer.

    RESULT
        Its offset; or MPEGA_ERR_NO_SYNC.

amcempega.library/MPEGA_open                     amcempega.library/MPEGA_open

    NAME
        MPEGA_open -- a stream opened (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        mpega_stream = MPEGA_open(stream_name, ctrl)
        D0                        A0           A1
        MPEGA_STREAM *MPEGA_open(char *, MPEGA_CTRL *);

    FUNCTION
        Opens the stream: through ctrl->bs_access, your hook (called with
        the hook in a0, the handle its MPEGA_BSFUNC_OPEN returned in a2,
        an MPEGA_ACCESS in a1: <libraries/mpega.h>), or, if that is NULL,
        the file stream_name. Passes over an ID3v2 tag, finds the first
        frame (with check_mpeg, a second of the same kind after it), reads
        a Xing or Info header, and fills in the MPEGA_STREAM: the stream's
        norm (MPEG-2.5's is 2), layer, mode, bitrate, frequency, channels,
        length (ms_duration: from the Xing header, else from the stream's
        size and bitrate), and what it decodes to (dec_channels,
        dec_frequency, dec_quality) from ctrl's settings for its layer:
        force_mono, then the mono or stereo MPEGA_OUTPUT's freq_div (1, 2
        or 4; any other: the least that keeps the rate at most freq_max)
        and quality. stream_buffer_size is the bytes read at a time (4096
        or more, else 16384).

    RESULT
        The stream; or NULL (not MPEG audio, no memory, no such file).

    NOTES
        Every quality decodes at the highest so far.

amcempega.library/MPEGA_scale                   amcempega.library/MPEGA_scale

    NAME
        MPEGA_scale -- the loudness set (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        error = MPEGA_scale(mpega_stream, scale_percent)
        D0                  A0            D0
        LONG MPEGA_scale(MPEGA_STREAM *, LONG);

    FUNCTION
        The samples scaled: 100 as decoded, 50 half, 200 twice (clipped).
        0 to 799.

    RESULT
        0; or MPEGA_ERR_BADVALUE.

amcempega.library/MPEGA_seek                     amcempega.library/MPEGA_seek

    NAME
        MPEGA_seek -- to a time in the stream (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        error = MPEGA_seek(mpega_stream, ms_time_position)
        D0                 A0            D0
        LONG MPEGA_seek(MPEGA_STREAM *, ULONG);

    FUNCTION
        The next MPEGA_decode_frame decodes from that time on: the place
        found from a Xing header's table, else from the bitrate, then the
        stream read from there (the hook's MPEGA_BSFUNC_SEEK, or the
        file's). The first frame or two after it may be passed over (the
        bit reservoir is not there yet).

    RESULT
        0; or MPEGA_ERR_EOF (past the end), MPEGA_ERR_BADVALUE (the stream
        cannot seek).

amcempega.library/MPEGA_time                     amcempega.library/MPEGA_time

    NAME
        MPEGA_time -- where the decoding is (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        error = MPEGA_time(mpega_stream, ms_time_position)
        D0                 A0            A1
        LONG MPEGA_time(MPEGA_STREAM *, ULONG *);

    FUNCTION
        The time of the samples given so far, in milliseconds (from the
        stream's start, or from where MPEGA_seek went).

    RESULT
        0; or MPEGA_ERR_BADVALUE.
